  "section_notes": "S5 sets an immediate 8-per-100,000 mandatory recall trigger with no transition, which would catch Halcyon's Ember 8 (9.9) and so weighs heavily against Halcyon. S3 gives installed units six years for retrofit, which favours Northwind's 38% shut-off coverage, while S2 bars public publication of per-model failure rates but requires numeric results to purchasers. S2 leaves the duration of the corrective-action plan for over-limit models unbounded, and S1 has no separate deadline for serious versus other incidents."
